<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Divico</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. 107–58 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Divico was a leader of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tigurini">Tigurini</a>, a Helvetian people, who defeated a Roman army under Lucius <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cassius-longinus">Cassius Longinus</a> near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/agen">Agen</a> in 107 BCE during the wars of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cimbri">Cimbri</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julius-caesar">Julius Caesar</a> records that, as an old man, he led the Helvetian embassy to Caesar in 58 BCE and defiantly reminded him of that earlier victory.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/divico.jpg" alt="Divico" width="320" height="413" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Charles Gleyre · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Charles_Gleyre_Les_Romans_p.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
